# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .gitignore for a VHDL / FPGA project
# Keeps source + curated reports; drops vendor-generated noise.
# Adjust to match the tools you actually use.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Xilinx Vivado ──
*.jou
*.log
*.str
*.backup.*
*.wdb
*.pb
*.dcp
.Xil/
*.cache/
*.hw/
*.ip_user_files/
*.runs/
*.sim/
*.gen/
usage_statistics_webtalk.*
vivado_pid*.str

# ── Intel/Altera Quartus ──
db/
incremental_db/
output_files/
*.qws
*.sof
*.pof
*.done
*.smsg
*.pin
*.qarlog
# NOTE: Quartus auto-generates *.rpt in output_files/. Your curated
# reports/ folder is committed separately and is NOT affected by the
# output_files/ rule above.

# ── ModelSim / Questa ──
work/
transcript
*.wlf
vsim.wlf
*.vstf
.vt/

# ── GHDL ──
*.cf
*.o
*.ghw
work-obj*.cf

# ── Bitstreams / large binaries (keep these out of git;
#    attach to a GitHub Release instead if you want to publish one) ──
*.bit
*.bin
*.rbf

# ── OS / editor cruft ──
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~
*.bak
*.tmp
.vscode/
.idea/
